## Bug found

`src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js` parsed the meridiem tokens `A`/`a` with hard-coded ASCII regexes and literal comparisons:

```js
const matchUpperCaseAMPM = /[AP]M/
const matchLowerCaseAMPM = /[ap]m/
...
A: [matchUpperCaseAMPM, function (input) { this.afternoon = input === 'PM' }],
a: [matchLowerCaseAMPM, function (input) { this.afternoon = input === 'pm' }],
```

When the active locale defines its own `meridiem` function (zh-cn/zh/ko/ja/br…), `format('A')` emits e.g. `上午`/`下午`, but parsing that string never matched `/[AP]M/` → `match[0]` threw inside `parseFormattedInput`'s try/catch → `new Date('')` → **Invalid Date**. Even if it had matched, the hard-coded `=== 'PM'` comparison ignored the locale's own meridiem strings.

## Fix applied (only `src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js`, 20 insertions / 6 deletions)

```diff
-const matchUpperCaseAMPM = /[AP]M/
-const matchLowerCaseAMPM = /[ap]m/
...
+const meridiemMatch = (input, isLowerCase) => {
+  let isAfternoon
+  const meridiem = locale && locale.meridiem
+  if (!meridiem) {
+    isAfternoon = input === (isLowerCase ? 'pm' : 'PM')
+  } else {
+    for (let i = 0; i <= 23; i += 1) {
+      if (input === meridiem(i, 0, isLowerCase)) {
+        isAfternoon = i > 11
+        break
+      }
+    }
+  }
+  return isAfternoon
+}
+
 const expressions = {
-  A: [matchUpperCaseAMPM, function (input) {
-    this.afternoon = input === 'PM'
+  A: [matchWord, function (input) {
+    this.afternoon = meridiemMatch(input, false)
   }],
-  a: [matchLowerCaseAMPM, function (input) {
-    this.afternoon = input === 'pm'
+  a: [matchWord, function (input) {
+    this.afternoon = meridiemMatch(input, true)
   }],
```

`matchWord` (`/\d*[^\s\d-:/()]+/`) is used so non-ASCII meridiem words are matched; `meridiemMatch` scans hours 0–23 (needed so zh-cn `下午`/`晚上`, which only occur for hours ≥ 13, resolve to afternoon) and falls back to the default `AM`/`PM` comparison when the locale has no `meridiem`. Existing `correctHours()` already does the right arithmetic (PM: +12 unless hour is 12; AM: hour 12 → 0), so it was left untouched.

## Verification

- Temp test `test/plugin/zz_meridiem_tmp.test.js` with tests named exactly `meridiem locale AM` / `meridiem locale PM` (zh-cn, `'2018-05-02 上午|下午 10:00'`, format `'YYYY-MM-DD A HH:mm'`, compared to moment, plus `hh` round trips and 12 AM→00 / 12 PM→12):
  - **With fix:** `PASS … ✓ meridiem locale AM ✓ meridiem locale PM — Test Suites: 1 passed, 1 total; Tests: 2 passed, 2 total`
  - **With fix reverted** (`git checkout`): both fail — `Expected value to be: 1525298400000, Received: NaN` (Invalid Date). Temp file deleted afterwards.
- Extra throwaway edge test (deleted): zh-cn 上午/下午/中午/晚上/凌晨/早上, 12-hour cases, ko 오전/오후, ja 午前/午後, br a.m./g.m., and `AM`/`PM` under zh-cn — all 18 cases `valueOf()` identical to moment 2.27.0.
- `npx eslint src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js` → clean (`LINT_OK`).
- Full suite `npx jest --coverage=false` → **Test Suites: 61 passed, 61 total; Tests: 529 passed, 529 total** (no failures; suite count grew from the baseline 58 only because colleagues' untracked `zz_*_tmp.test.js` files are present — none of my changes touch them).
- Also re-ran `customParseFormat.test.js` + `zh-cn.test.js` under TZ=Pacific/Auckland, Europe/London, America/Whitehorse: 39/39 pass each.

No pre-existing test file was modified; only `src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js` was changed (the other dirty files `src/locale/nl.js`, `src/plugin/timezone/index.js` are colleagues' pre-existing edits, untouched by me).

